DeliveryApp — unrelated regression candidate observed during AC7 signed-out routing check
(NOT caused by NEARS-3004's Timer-budget change; splash_screen.dart's routing-decision code
untouched by this diff — only the Timer duration changed).

Repro: Profile > Logout > Yes (navigated to sign-in screen immediately), then force-stop + cold
start (adb shell am start -W) shortly after.

Observed: on the next cold start, isLoggedIn() still reported true (stale local flag), so
_handleDefaultRouting() attempted the logged-in branch, hit 401s on every authenticated endpoint,
and looped repeated POST /api/v1/delivery-man/logout calls (5x in ~1s) before the app's 401
interceptor eventually routed to sign-in:

  09:39:17.635 [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/config http_status=200
  09:39:17.640 [NET] GET endpoint=/api/v1/delivery-man/profile
  09:39:18.660 [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/delivery-man/profile http_status=401
  09:39:18.669 [NET] POST endpoint=/api/v1/delivery-man/logout
  09:39:19.524 [NET] POST endpoint=/api/v1/delivery-man/logout
  09:39:19.527 [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/delivery-man/latest-orders http_status=401
  09:39:19.657 [NET] POST endpoint=/api/v1/delivery-man/logout
  09:39:19.732/.789/.856/20.606 endpoint=/api/v1/delivery-man/logout http_status=401 (x4 more)

End state was correct (landed on sign-in screen), so this did not block AC7, but the repeated
401-triggered logout calls suggest either a logout-flow race (navigating before local token clear
completes) or the 401 interceptor firing once per failed endpoint instead of once globally. Not
part of this ticket's blast radius (splash Timer only) — flagged as a regression candidate for the
PO, not filed as a task_bug against NEARS-3004.
